# Keep the web/ directory in git even when empty.
#
# The Go embed directive `//go:embed web` in cmd/server/main.go
# requires the pattern to match at least one file at compile time.
# In a fresh clone (e.g. CI before the frontend has been built),
# `web/` is empty because everything in it is generated. Without
# this file, `go build` / `go test` fails with:
#   pattern web: no matching files found
# Once `release.sh` (or `frontend` build) runs, it populates `web/`
# with the real SPA bundle, and this `.gitkeep` is harmless leftover
# that the static middleware never serves.
